# Docs: Base UI handoff Card

When a **ComponentPage** documents a Vira surface that wraps a Base UI **component primitive**, put a Base UI handoff Card **at the top of the page body** — immediately after frontmatter, before the lead narrative. Contract: `specs/001-llm-first-docs-site/contracts/page-shell.md`.

## Authority (do not invent)

Read sibling DS agent-doc specs — **not** memory, Storybook, or Base UI site browsing:

1. `../vira-ui/packages/react/src/components/<id>/specs/meta.xml`
2. Copy `<base_ui href="…"/>` **verbatim** into the Card `href` (keep `#api-reference`)
3. If meta has `shared_contract="<other-id>"` and no own `<base_ui>`, resolve that unit’s `<base_ui>` (e.g. IconButton → Button)
4. No `<base_ui>` after resolve → **omit** the Card (Vira-only / `use-render` helpers)

Published mirror when checkout unavailable: `@viraui/react/specs` / guide `baseUIApi` — same URL.

## When omit

- No `<base_ui>` in meta (and none via `shared_contract`)
- ViraUI-only surfaces; helpers that only use `use-render` / `merge-props`

## Shape

```mdx
## Base UI

<Cards>
  <Card
    title="Button"
    href="https://base-ui.com/react/components/button#api-reference"
    external
  >
    Upstream API and behavior for the Base UI primitive this control wraps.
  </Card>
</Cards>
```

## Rules

- `href` = exact meta `<base_ui href>` (or resolved shared_contract target) — never hand-map Dialog→Drawer etc. from memory
- `title` = Base UI component name derived from that URL’s last path segment (e.g. `drawer` → `Drawer`, `toggle-group` → `Toggle Group`)
- Always set `external` on the Card
- One Card only; no “What’s next” tour
- Voice stays consumer-facing; Card body explains upstream pass-through, not authoring instructions
